        "##4. Create a Mermaid Flow Chart for an Algorithm"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "tiOjsggHPrr6"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Purpose:** Learn how to graphically communicate the flow of a computer program or its underlying algorithms via flow charts.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Task**:\n",
        "1. Create a Mermaid Script to Generate a Flow Chart that visually presents the following algorithm\n",
        "    ```\n",
        "    def matmul(A, B):\n",
        "        # A is m×n, B is n×p\n",
        "        m, n = len(A), len(A[0])\n",
        "        p = len(B[0])\n",
        "\n",
        "        # initialise result matrix with zeros\n",
        "        C = [[0 for _ in range(p)] for _ in range(m)]\n",
        "\n",
        "        # triple‑loop multiplication\n",
        "        for i in range(m):\n",
        "            for j in range(p):\n",
        "                s = 0\n",
        "                for k in range(n):\n",
        "                    s += A[i][k] * B[k][j]\n",
        "                C[i][j] = s\n",
        "\n",
        "        return C\n",
        "    ```\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Modify the flow chart to ensure it fits with standard conventions (see [Notebook 1.3 - Documenting and Communicating Code](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/16XTGJmcjxi0CU_MRgGw0hdmuXAoXvi-R?usp=playground))\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Use the **colab-print** library to render the Flow Chart within the Colab environment.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal**: Get comfortable using flow-charts to communicate the flow of algorithms and be able to efficiently generate them to help document and explain a digital work flow."
      ],
